# LF in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# `text=auto` on its own normalises to LF when committing but still checks out
# CRLF on Windows. That breaks this project rather than merely annoying it: the
# working tree is bind-mounted into a Linux container, and a CRLF
# entrypoint.sh fails at startup with "bad interpreter". `eol=lf` pins the
# working tree too, so a Windows clone runs the same bytes as CI.
* text=auto eol=lf
